<section id="update">
  <p class="kicker">skyBlip Go</p>
  <h1>New firmware, from this page, over Bluetooth.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Nothing to install and nothing to pair. The page sends the image, and the
    device asks you on its own glass twice: before it takes the image, and
    before it installs it. A phone cannot update it on its own.
  </p>

  <%= render "shared/manage",
        unsupported: "This browser has no Web Bluetooth, so this page cannot reach the device. Use Chrome or Edge, on a computer or on Android. Safari, Firefox, and every browser on an iPhone or an iPad lack it.",
        connect: "Connect",
        disconnect: "Disconnect",
        connecting: "Your browser lists the devices in range: pick skyBlip Go followed by its address.",
        device: "Device",
        firmware: "Running",
        battery: "Battery",
        charging: "charging",
        chosen: "Chosen image",
        file: "The firmware file, ending in .signed.bin",
        install: "Install",
        steps: {
          dfu: "Allow the upload: the glass says FIRMWARE, press twice.",
          upload: "The image travels. Keep this page open and the device close.",
          apply: "Allow the install: the glass says INSTALL, press twice.",
          install: "The device installs and restarts, about thirty seconds, and the link drops. Connect again to see the result."
        },
        remaining: "about %{minutes} min left",
        recovery: "If the firmware will not take: the USB drive",
        confirm_recovery: "The glass says RECOVERY, REBOOT INTO THE USB BOOTLOADER: press twice.",
        recovering: "The glass now says USB BOOTLOADER. If it reads PRESS THE BUTTON TO START IT, press the button once. On a computer the device is then a USB drive named TECHOBOOT: drop the .uf2 file on it for new firmware, or press RST to go back to skyBlip. Nothing transmits meanwhile.",
