<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">Before you start</h2>

  <ul class="points">
    <li>Chrome or Edge, on a computer or on Android</li>
    <li>The device on the ground, with a GPS fix</li>
    <li>A battery above the warning, or charging</li>
    <li>The release file ending in .signed.bin</li>
    <li>No other app holding the device&rsquo;s settings</li>
    <li>Ten minutes, with the device close to you</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">What happens</h2>

  <h3>Two questions on the glass, <span class="highlight">one upload between them</span>.</h3>
  <p class="lede">
    Install first asks the device to accept an image. The glass says
    <span class="mono">FIRMWARE</span>,
    <span class="mono">LET THE PHONE WRITE A NEW IMAGE</span>: press twice. That
    opens a window of ten minutes, and only while the device knows it is on the
    ground.
  </p>
  <p class="lede">
    The image travels next, and the page shows how much of it has arrived. The
    window closes at ten minutes, at a take-off, or when the link drops. Install
    again and the upload picks up where it stopped, as long as the device has
    not restarted in between.
  </p>
  <p class="lede">
    Once the last byte is in, the page asks for the install. The glass says
    <span class="mono">INSTALL</span>,
    <span class="mono">REBOOT INTO THE STAGED IMAGE</span>: press twice again.
    The device paints <span class="mono">INSTALLING</span> and restarts into the
    new firmware, which takes about thirty seconds, and the link drops.
  </p>
  <p class="lede">
    Connect again. The new firmware starts on probation: it has to bring its
    radio up, hear its GPS receiver and draw its screen before it keeps itself.
    If it does not, the device goes back to the firmware it had, and this page
    says so rather than leave you looking at an old version number.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">What it tells you about itself</h2>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="modules">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>The device reports</th><th>What it means</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th class="mono">probation</th><td data-manage-word="probation">The new firmware is proving itself: radio up, receiver talking, screen drawn. This resolves on its own within seconds, there is nothing to do.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">reverted</th><td data-manage-word="reverted">The last update did not take, and the device went back to the firmware it had. Nothing is broken: the version number is the old one on purpose. Try again, and if it happens twice, tell us which version you tried.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">settings: prior</th><td data-manage-word="settings_prior">Your settings are the ones from before that update: what you changed while the newer firmware ran stayed with it.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">settings: defaults</th><td data-manage-word="settings_defaults">The stored settings could not be read, so the device runs on its defaults. Check the callsign and the aircraft type before you fly.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">swap_powered: false</th><td data-manage-word="swap_unpowered">The battery is below the warning, too low to install. Charge it first.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">went_dark_flat</th><td data-manage-word="went_dark_flat">The last time it switched off, it was for a flat battery. Charge it before you update.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">When it says no</h2>

  <p class="lede">
    Every refusal comes with a reason, and the page puts it in the words below.
  </p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="modules">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>The device answers</th><th>What it means, and what to do</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th class="mono">in_flight</th><td data-manage-word="in_flight">It has not proven it is on the ground: it is flying, or has had no GPS fix since it was switched on. Take it where it sees the sky, wait for the fix, then try again.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">low_power</th><td data-manage-word="low_power">The battery is below the warning. Installing is 15 to 25 seconds of flash erases, and the device does not start one on a cell that might not finish it. Charge it, then try again.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">expired</th><td data-manage-word="expired">Nobody answered the question on the glass within thirty seconds, which counts as a refusal. Try again, and press twice when the glass asks.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">cancelled</th><td data-manage-word="cancelled">The question was refused on the device: one press says no.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">nothing_staged</th><td data-manage-word="nothing_staged">No new firmware is waiting on the device. Install again to send the image.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">upload_unfinished</th><td data-manage-word="upload_unfinished">The image did not arrive whole since the window opened, or the device restarted after it arrived. Install again to send it.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">claimed</th><td data-manage-word="claimed">Another app holds this device&rsquo;s settings. Disconnect it or close it, then connect again.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">window_closed</th><td data-manage-word="window_closed">The upload window closed: it lasts ten minutes, and a take-off, a refusal on the glass or a dropped link closes it sooner. Install again: the upload picks up where it stopped, unless the device restarted.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">not_newer</th><td data-manage-word="not_newer">The device already runs this version or a newer one, and it never goes back to an older one.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">too_large</th><td data-manage-word="too_large">This image is bigger than the room the device keeps for an update, so it is not a skyBlip Go image.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">not_image</th><td data-manage-word="not_image">This file is not a signed firmware image. Choose the one ending in .signed.bin: the .uf2 is for the USB drive.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">flash</th><td data-manage-word="flash">The device could not write the image to its memory. Try again, and if it happens again, use the USB drive.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">unknown_cmd</th><td data-manage-word="unknown_cmd">The firmware on the device is older than this page and does not know the question. Update it with the USB drive.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">anything else</th><td data-manage-word="refused">The device refused, with a reason this page does not know:</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">When the page stops</h2>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="modules">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>The page says</th><th>What it means, and what to do</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>No Web Bluetooth</th><td data-manage-word="no_bluetooth">This browser has no Web Bluetooth. Use Chrome or Edge, on a computer or on Android. Safari, Firefox, and every browser on an iPhone or an iPad lack it.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Not a skyBlip</th><td data-manage-word="not_skyblip">The device you picked has no firmware update service: it is not a skyBlip, or its firmware predates updates over Bluetooth.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>No file</th><td data-manage-word="no_file">Choose the firmware file first.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Link lost</th><td data-manage-word="link_lost">The link dropped. Bring the device closer and connect again: an upload under way picks up where it stopped.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>No answer</th><td data-manage-word="timeout">The device stopped answering. Disconnect, connect again, and install again.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>No room given</th><td data-manage-word="no_params">The device did not say how much of the image it takes at once. Disconnect and connect again.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Refused</th><td data-manage-word="smp">The device refused the image with an error this page does not know:</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Anything else</th><td data-manage-word="failed">Something failed on the way:</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">Without this page</h2>

  <h3>Press <span class="mono">RST</span> twice, and <span class="highlight">it is a USB drive</span>.</h3>
  <p class="lede">
    Twice inside half a second, with the device on a USB cable. It shows up on
    the computer as a drive named <span class="mono">TECHOBOOT</span>: drop the
    <span class="mono">.uf2</span> file of a release on it, and the device
    restarts on that firmware. That road needs no browser at all, and it is the
    one to take when the firmware on the device will not answer this page.
  </p>
</section>

